From ef481b0c0a72e90f316a54020dd1969598d42118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:45:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] osvlocal: a configured vendor source is matched next to
 api.osv.dev

A vendor family whose archive location was given in the Options
(VendorFeeds, else VendorURL) is "configured" (Options.Configured) and must
not be silently ignored in online scans:

* Options.MatchedLocally reports the ecosystems the enricher handles with
  LocalOnlyEcosystems: those api.osv.dev does not serve and now also the
  configured vendor families.
* vulnmatch/osvdev gets Configure(Options{MatchedLocally}): those
  ecosystems are left out of the batch query.
* An unavailable configured archive follows the rule of a built-in default:
  a warning naming the source, and the enricher goes on; VendorStrict makes
  it an error.
* VendorStrict is not satisfied by a cached copy: the cache is keyed by
  ecosystem, not by source, so the copy may be stale or from another
  source; a failed fetch is reported instead (zipDB.NoCacheFallback).
  Without strict mode the cached copy is used with a warning, as before.
* A file:// archive is read before the Offline check: a local source is no
  download, so a directory of archives works when downloads are off.

The apk test cases apply only while the module names the distributions
osv-scalibr and osv-schema know (distroKnown).
